cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "polar-hrv-viz: visualisation of heart rate, RR intervals and motion from Polar optical sensors"
abstract: >-
  A small Python package and command line tool that loads heart rate,
  RR interval and accelerometer recordings from a Polar optical sensor,
  flags artifacts, summarises each phase of an experiment and renders
  timeline, RR histogram, Poincaré and per-phase heart rate figures.
  Developed as part of research on multimodal emotional AI for assessing
  the professional preparation of educators.
